    "title": "Frog Jump",
    "category": "Dynamic Programming",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "A frog stands on the first stone and wants to reach the last stone. Each stone has a height. The frog may jump to the next stone or skip one stone. The energy cost of a jump is the absolute difference between the heights of the two stones. Determine the minimum total energy required.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integer N. \u2022 Second line contains N integers representing stone heights.",
    "output": "Print the minimum total energy.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 2 \u2264 N \u2264 2\u00d710^5"
